Inet server protocol helpers — ARP + ICMP + link-layer glue
=============================================================

Companion to `oskit/servers/inet.lsysl`. Split out so the
larger wire-format logic doesn't crowd the socket-API file.
Both files share `module oskit.servers`.

This file owns:

- Our IP + gateway IP + MAC state
- ARP request / reply builders + ICMP echo request / reply
  builders
- `inet_handle_frame()` — EtherType dispatch on inbound frames
- Thin nic-client wrappers — inet is an isolated server and can't
  import `oskit.ulib` (that's for user programs), so we duplicate
  the four nic IPC wrappers here against `oskit.ipc.ipc_send`.

Replaces `oskit/drivers/virtio/net_handler.lsysl`, which used to
live in kernel-thread space and call `virtio_net_send` directly.

    module oskit.servers

    import oskit.ipc.{ipc_send, port_lookup, ipc_reply}
    import oskit.services.uptime
    import std.net.{ETHERTYPE_IPV4, ETHERTYPE_ARP,
        ARP_OP_REQUEST, ARP_OP_REPLY,
        IP_PROTO_ICMP, IP_PROTO_UDP, IP_PROTO_TCP,
        ICMP_ECHO_REQ, ICMP_ECHO_REP,
        pkt_read_u16, pkt_write_u16,
        pkt_write_mac, pkt_write_ipv4,
        pkt_match_ipv4, net_checksum,
        ipv4, ipv4_octet}


The guest's IP and gateway IP under QEMU user-mode networking.
Hardcoded to QEMU's default `-netdev user` lease (every guest
gets the same lease so this is fine for bring-up).

    val INET_OUR_IP_A = 10
    val INET_OUR_IP_B = 0
    val INET_OUR_IP_C = 2
    val INET_OUR_IP_D = 15

    val INET_GW_IP_A = 10
    val INET_GW_IP_B = 0
    val INET_GW_IP_C = 2
    val INET_GW_IP_D = 2


Link-layer state. `inet_our_mac_known` guards every outbound
build because the nic may not be available (e.g. on x86 builds
where the virtio-net stack isn't wired in).

    var inet_our_mac: [6]byte
    var inet_our_mac_known: int = 0


### ARP cache

16-entry (IP, MAC) table shared by every outbound send. Replaces
the previous `inet_gw_mac + inet_gw_mac_known` pair so the stack
can talk to peers other than the default gateway once their MAC
has been learned via ARP. Full cache evicts slot 0 (FIFO-ish —
promote to LRU if traffic starts churning).

    val INET_ARP_SIZE = 16

    struct InetArpEntry
        ip: u32
        mac: [6]byte
        in_use: int

    var inet_arp_cache: [16]InetArpEntry


Slot index for `ip`, or -1 if not cached.

    inet_arp_lookup_idx(ip: u32) -> int
        var i = 0
        while i < INET_ARP_SIZE
            if inet_arp_cache[i].in_use != 0
                if inet_arp_cache[i].ip == ip
                    return i
            i += 1
        -1


Copy the cached MAC for `ip` into `out`. Returns 1 on hit, 0 on
miss (in which case `out` is untouched).

    inet_arp_lookup(ip: u32, out: *byte) -> int
        val idx = inet_arp_lookup_idx(ip)
        if idx < 0
            return 0
        var j = 0
        while j < 6
            out[j] = inet_arp_cache[idx].mac[j]
            j += 1
        1


Insert or update (ip, mac). Re-use an existing slot for `ip` if
present; otherwise grab the first free slot; otherwise evict
slot 0 (simplest FIFO-ish policy). Good enough at this scale.

    inet_arp_insert(ip: u32, mac: *byte)
        var idx = inet_arp_lookup_idx(ip)
        if idx < 0
            var i = 0
            while i < INET_ARP_SIZE
                if inet_arp_cache[i].in_use == 0
                    idx = i
                    i = INET_ARP_SIZE
                else
                    i += 1
        if idx < 0
            idx = 0
        inet_arp_cache[idx].ip = ip
        var j = 0
        while j < 6
            inet_arp_cache[idx].mac[j] = mac[j]
            j += 1
        inet_arp_cache[idx].in_use = 1


Returns 1 if `ip` lives in our local /24 subnet (matches our
first 3 octets). Off-subnet destinations route via the default
gateway.

    inet_in_subnet(ip: u32) -> int
        if ipv4_octet(ip, 0) != INET_OUR_IP_A
            return 0
        if ipv4_octet(ip, 1) != INET_OUR_IP_B
            return 0
        if ipv4_octet(ip, 2) != INET_OUR_IP_C
            return 0
        1


Resolve the next-hop MAC for `dst_ip`: the cached entry for
`dst_ip` itself if on-subnet, otherwise the default gateway's
entry. On miss, fires an ARP request for the target and returns
0 — caller drops the packet (UDP best-effort). Returns 1 on hit
with `out` filled.

    inet_resolve_mac(dst_ip: u32, out: *byte) -> int
        var target_ip = dst_ip
        if inet_in_subnet(dst_ip) == 0
            target_ip = ipv4(INET_GW_IP_A, INET_GW_IP_B,
                INET_GW_IP_C, INET_GW_IP_D)
        if inet_arp_lookup(target_ip, out) != 0
            return 1
        inet_send_arp_request(
            ipv4_octet(target_ip, 0), ipv4_octet(target_ip, 1),
            ipv4_octet(target_ip, 2), ipv4_octet(target_ip, 3))
        0


Diagnostic counters. Useful for asserting the TX / RX loop is
flowing end-to-end during bring-up.

    var inet_pings_sent: int = 0
    var inet_pings_received: int = 0


NIC command codes — must track `oskit/servers/nic.lsysl`.

    val INET_NIC_CMD_GET_MAC      = 1
    val INET_NIC_CMD_SEND_PACKET  = 2
    val INET_NIC_CMD_SUBSCRIBE_RX = 3
    val INET_NIC_CMD_RECV_PACKET  = 4


Cached nic port, resolved lazily on first use. -1 means both
"not yet looked up" and "lookup failed" — callers always re-try
on -1 so a nic that comes up late (future: restartable) still
gets picked up.

    var inet_nic_port = -1

    inet_nic_get_port() -> int
        if inet_nic_port < 0
            inet_nic_port = port_lookup("nic")
        inet_nic_port


### inet_nic_get_mac

Writes 6 MAC bytes into `out`. 0 on success, -1 on any failure.

    inet_nic_get_mac(out: *byte) -> int
        val port = inet_nic_get_port()
        if port < 0
            return -1
        var msg: [1]byte
        msg[0] = byte(INET_NIC_CMD_GET_MAC)
        var reply: [7]byte
        val r = ipc_send(port, msg, 1, reply, 7)
        if r < 0
            return -1
        if int(reply[0]) != 0
            return -1
        var i = 0
        while i < 6
            out[i] = reply[1 + i]
            i += 1
        0


### inet_nic_send_packet

Submits a raw Ethernet frame to the nic's TX path. 0 on success,
-1 on any error.

    inet_nic_send_packet(frame: *byte, len: int) -> int
        val port = inet_nic_get_port()
        if port < 0
            return -1
        if len <= 0 || len > 1514
            return -1
        var msg: [1520]byte
        msg[0] = byte(INET_NIC_CMD_SEND_PACKET)
        msg[1] = byte((len >> 8) & 0xff)
        msg[2] = byte(len & 0xff)
        var i = 0
        while i < len
            msg[3 + i] = frame[i]
            i += 1
        var reply: [1]byte
        val r = ipc_send(port, msg, 3 + len, reply, 1)
        if r < 0
            return -1
        if int(reply[0]) != 0
            return -1
        0


### inet_nic_subscribe_rx

Registers this server's main thread as the nic's sole RX
notification target. 0 on success, -1 on any error.

    inet_nic_subscribe_rx() -> int
        val port = inet_nic_get_port()
        if port < 0
            return -1
        var msg: [1]byte
        msg[0] = byte(INET_NIC_CMD_SUBSCRIBE_RX)
        var reply: [1]byte
        val r = ipc_send(port, msg, 1, reply, 1)
        if r < 0
            return -1
        if int(reply[0]) != 0
            return -1
        0


### inet_nic_recv_packet

Non-blocking pop of the head of the nic's RX queue. Returns the
frame's raw length (up to `maxlen` bytes copied into `out`), or
-1 when the queue is empty / on IPC failure.

    inet_nic_recv_packet(out: *byte, maxlen: int) -> int
        val port = inet_nic_get_port()
        if port < 0
            return -1
        if maxlen < 0
            return -1
        var msg: [1]byte
        msg[0] = byte(INET_NIC_CMD_RECV_PACKET)
        var reply: [1517]byte
        val r = ipc_send(port, msg, 1, reply, 1517)
        if r < 0
            return -1
        if int(reply[0]) != 0
            return -1
        val raw_len = ((int(reply[1]) & 0xff) << 8) | (int(reply[2]) & 0xff)
        var take = raw_len
        if take > maxlen
            take = maxlen
        var i = 0
        while i < take
            out[i] = reply[3 + i]
            i += 1
        raw_len


### Link-layer state setters

    inet_set_our_mac(mac: *byte)
        var i = 0
        while i < 6
            inet_our_mac[i] = mac[i]
            i += 1
        inet_our_mac_known = 1

    inet_bump_pings_received()
        inet_pings_received += 1


ARP request for the IPv4 address `ta.tb.tc.td`, broadcast. Uses
our MAC (must be known — early-returns -1 otherwise). Returns 0
on success, -1 on failure.

    inet_send_arp_request(ta: int, tb: int, tc: int, td: int) -> int
        if inet_our_mac_known == 0
            return -1
        var frame: [42]byte
        var i = 0
        while i < 6
            frame[i] = 0xff
            i += 1
        pkt_write_mac(frame, 6, inet_our_mac)
        pkt_write_u16(frame, 12, ETHERTYPE_ARP)
        pkt_write_u16(frame, 14, 1)              // htype = Ethernet
        pkt_write_u16(frame, 16, ETHERTYPE_IPV4) // ptype = IPv4
        frame[18] = 6                            // hlen
        frame[19] = 4                            // plen
        pkt_write_u16(frame, 20, ARP_OP_REQUEST)
        pkt_write_mac(frame, 22, inet_our_mac)
        pkt_write_ipv4(frame, 28,
            INET_OUR_IP_A, INET_OUR_IP_B, INET_OUR_IP_C, INET_OUR_IP_D)
        i = 0
        while i < 6
            frame[32 + i] = 0
            i += 1
        pkt_write_ipv4(frame, 38, ta, tb, tc, td)
        inet_nic_send_packet(frame, 42)


ARP reply. `req` points at the start of the Ethernet frame that
carried the request; senders from the request become targets in
the reply.

    inet_send_arp_reply(req: *byte) -> int
        if inet_our_mac_known == 0
            return -1
        var frame: [42]byte
        pkt_write_mac(frame, 0, req + 22)       // dst = requester's MAC
        pkt_write_mac(frame, 6, inet_our_mac)   // src = us
        pkt_write_u16(frame, 12, ETHERTYPE_ARP)
        pkt_write_u16(frame, 14, 1)
        pkt_write_u16(frame, 16, ETHERTYPE_IPV4)
        frame[18] = 6
        frame[19] = 4
        pkt_write_u16(frame, 20, ARP_OP_REPLY)
        pkt_write_mac(frame, 22, inet_our_mac)
        pkt_write_ipv4(frame, 28,
            INET_OUR_IP_A, INET_OUR_IP_B, INET_OUR_IP_C, INET_OUR_IP_D)
        pkt_write_mac(frame, 32, req + 22)      // target MAC = requester
        pkt_write_ipv4(frame, 38,
            int(req[28]) & 0xff,
            int(req[29]) & 0xff,
            int(req[30]) & 0xff,
            int(req[31]) & 0xff)
        inet_nic_send_packet(frame, 42)


ICMP echo request to the gateway. Destination MAC must already
have been learned via ARP. `id` + `seq` are reflected by the peer
in its reply so we can match replies to requests.

    inet_send_icmp_echo(id: int, seq: int) -> int
        if inet_our_mac_known == 0
            return -1
        var gw_mac: [6]byte
        val gw_ip = ipv4(INET_GW_IP_A, INET_GW_IP_B,
            INET_GW_IP_C, INET_GW_IP_D)
        if inet_arp_lookup(gw_ip, gw_mac) == 0
            return -1
        var frame: [42]byte

Ethernet header.

        pkt_write_mac(frame, 0, gw_mac)
        pkt_write_mac(frame, 6, inet_our_mac)
        pkt_write_u16(frame, 12, ETHERTYPE_IPV4)

IPv4 header (20 bytes, no options).

        frame[14] = 0x45                         // version 4, IHL 5
        frame[15] = 0                            // DSCP/ECN
        pkt_write_u16(frame, 16, 28)             // total length = 20 + 8
        pkt_write_u16(frame, 18, 0)              // id
        pkt_write_u16(frame, 20, 0)              // flags + frag = 0
        frame[22] = 64                           // TTL
        frame[23] = byte(IP_PROTO_ICMP)
        pkt_write_u16(frame, 24, 0)              // checksum placeholder
        pkt_write_ipv4(frame, 26,
            INET_OUR_IP_A, INET_OUR_IP_B, INET_OUR_IP_C, INET_OUR_IP_D)
        pkt_write_ipv4(frame, 30,
            INET_GW_IP_A, INET_GW_IP_B, INET_GW_IP_C, INET_GW_IP_D)
        pkt_write_u16(frame, 24, net_checksum(frame + 14, 20))

ICMP echo (8 bytes, no payload).

        frame[34] = byte(ICMP_ECHO_REQ)
        frame[35] = 0                            // code
        pkt_write_u16(frame, 36, 0)              // checksum placeholder
        pkt_write_u16(frame, 38, id)
        pkt_write_u16(frame, 40, seq)
        pkt_write_u16(frame, 36, net_checksum(frame + 34, 8))

        val r = inet_nic_send_packet(frame, 42)
        if r == 0
            inet_pings_sent += 1
        r


ICMP echo reply in response to `req`. `req` points at the start
of the Ethernet frame (ICMP payload starts at offset 14 + ihl).

    inet_send_icmp_reply(req: *byte, total_len: int) -> int
        if inet_our_mac_known == 0
            return -1
        var frame: [1514]byte
        if total_len > 1514
            return -1
        if total_len < 14 + 20 + 8
            return -1

Copy the whole request into our buffer as a starting point; we
then rewrite the bits that change between request and reply.

        var i = 0
        while i < total_len
            frame[i] = req[i]
            i += 1

Ethernet: swap src and dst.

        pkt_write_mac(frame, 0, req + 6)
        pkt_write_mac(frame, 6, inet_our_mac)

IPv4: swap src and dst IP, zero checksum, recompute.

        var j = 0
        while j < 4
            frame[14 + 12 + j] = req[14 + 16 + j]   // dst <- old src
            frame[14 + 16 + j] = req[14 + 12 + j]   // src <- old dst
            j += 1
        pkt_write_u16(frame, 14 + 10, 0)
        val ihl_bytes = (int(frame[14]) & 0x0f) * 4
        pkt_write_u16(frame, 14 + 10, net_checksum(frame + 14, ihl_bytes))

ICMP: flip type from echo-request to echo-reply, zero checksum,
recompute over the full ICMP message.

        val icmp_off = 14 + ihl_bytes
        frame[icmp_off] = byte(ICMP_ECHO_REP)
        pkt_write_u16(frame, icmp_off + 2, 0)
        val icmp_len = total_len - icmp_off
        pkt_write_u16(frame, icmp_off + 2,
            net_checksum(frame + icmp_off, icmp_len))

        inet_nic_send_packet(frame, total_len)


### L4 checksum helpers (IPv4 pseudo-header)

Core one's-complement sum over `pseudo-header + L4 header +
payload`. Pseudo-header layout (12 bytes): src_ip (4) + dst_ip
(4) + zero (1) + proto (1) + l4_len (2). The L4 bytes come
straight from the frame buffer at `[l4_off .. l4_off + l4_len)`
— caller decides whether the checksum field there is zero (for
transmit) or stored (for receive-side verify).

Returns the folded 16-bit sum (not complemented). Valid transmit
frames have the complement stored in their checksum field;
receive-side verification expects this helper to return `0xffff`
when the stored checksum is correct. Shared by UDP (proto=17)
and TCP (proto=6).

    inet_l4_partial_sum(src_ip: u32, dst_ip: u32, proto: int,
                        frame: *byte, l4_off: int, l4_len: int) -> int
        var sum = 0
        sum += (ipv4_octet(src_ip, 0) << 8) | ipv4_octet(src_ip, 1)
        sum += (ipv4_octet(src_ip, 2) << 8) | ipv4_octet(src_ip, 3)
        sum += (ipv4_octet(dst_ip, 0) << 8) | ipv4_octet(dst_ip, 1)
        sum += (ipv4_octet(dst_ip, 2) << 8) | ipv4_octet(dst_ip, 3)
        sum += proto
        sum += l4_len
        var i = 0
        while i + 1 < l4_len
            sum += pkt_read_u16(frame, l4_off + i)
            i += 2
        if i < l4_len
            sum += (int(frame[l4_off + i]) & 0xff) << 8
        while (sum >> 16) != 0
            sum = (sum & 0xffff) + (sum >> 16)
        sum


Transmit-side helper. Caller must zero the UDP checksum field in
`frame` before calling. A computed 0 maps to `0xffff` so the
written value never collides with the "no checksum" sentinel
(RFC 768).

    inet_udp_checksum(src_ip: u32, dst_ip: u32,
                     frame: *byte, udp_off: int, udp_len: int) -> int
        val s = inet_l4_partial_sum(src_ip, dst_ip, IP_PROTO_UDP,
                                    frame, udp_off, udp_len)
        val c = (~s) & 0xffff
        if c == 0
            return 0xffff
        c


Receive-side verify. Frame still carries its sender-written
checksum; a valid packet folds to `0xffff`. A stored 0 means
"no checksum" (accept unconditionally, IPv4-only). Returns 1
on valid, 0 on corrupt.

    inet_udp_verify(src_ip: u32, dst_ip: u32,
                   frame: *byte, udp_off: int, udp_len: int) -> int
        val stored = pkt_read_u16(frame, udp_off + 6)
        if stored == 0
            return 1
        val s = inet_l4_partial_sum(src_ip, dst_ip, IP_PROTO_UDP,
                                    frame, udp_off, udp_len)
        if s == 0xffff
            return 1
        0


### UDP — outbound

Builds a full Ethernet/IPv4/UDP frame and hands it to the nic.
`inet_resolve_mac` picks the next-hop MAC: the destination's own
cached MAC for on-subnet targets, the gateway's for off-subnet.
Cache miss fires an ARP request and returns -1 (UDP semantics let
the caller retry). Also returns -1 if the link isn't ready,
`dlen` is out of range, or the nic rejects the frame.

UDP checksum is computed over the IPv4 pseudo-header + UDP header
+ payload — required for IPv6 peers and recommended for IPv4.

    inet_send_udp(dst_ip: u32, dst_port: int, src_port: int, data: *byte, dlen: int) -> int
        if inet_our_mac_known == 0
            return -1
        if dlen < 0
            return -1
        if dlen > 1472
            return -1
        var next_hop_mac: [6]byte
        if inet_resolve_mac(dst_ip, next_hop_mac) == 0
            return -1
        var frame: [1514]byte
        val total_len = 14 + 20 + 8 + dlen

Ethernet header.

        pkt_write_mac(frame, 0, next_hop_mac)
        pkt_write_mac(frame, 6, inet_our_mac)
        pkt_write_u16(frame, 12, ETHERTYPE_IPV4)

IPv4 header (20 bytes, no options).

        frame[14] = 0x45
        frame[15] = 0
        pkt_write_u16(frame, 16, 20 + 8 + dlen)
        pkt_write_u16(frame, 18, 0)
        pkt_write_u16(frame, 20, 0)
        frame[22] = 64
        frame[23] = byte(IP_PROTO_UDP)
        pkt_write_u16(frame, 24, 0)
        pkt_write_ipv4(frame, 26,
            INET_OUR_IP_A, INET_OUR_IP_B, INET_OUR_IP_C, INET_OUR_IP_D)
        pkt_write_ipv4(frame, 30, ipv4_octet(dst_ip, 0), ipv4_octet(dst_ip, 1), ipv4_octet(dst_ip, 2), ipv4_octet(dst_ip, 3))
        pkt_write_u16(frame, 24, net_checksum(frame + 14, 20))

UDP header + payload. Checksum field is zeroed before computing
the pseudo-header checksum; the result lands at offset 40.

        pkt_write_u16(frame, 34, src_port)
        pkt_write_u16(frame, 36, dst_port)
        pkt_write_u16(frame, 38, 8 + dlen)
        pkt_write_u16(frame, 40, 0)
        var i = 0
        while i < dlen
            frame[42 + i] = data[i]
            i += 1
        val our_ip = ipv4(INET_OUR_IP_A, INET_OUR_IP_B,
            INET_OUR_IP_C, INET_OUR_IP_D)
        pkt_write_u16(frame, 40,
            inet_udp_checksum(our_ip, dst_ip, frame, 34, 8 + dlen))

        inet_nic_send_packet(frame, total_len)


### TCP — state machine (phase 1 MVP)

Active-open client only. `connect()` → SYN_SENT → ESTABLISHED,
graceful close either side, fixed 500 ms RTO, TIME_WAIT capped
at 2 s. No listen/accept, no out-of-order reassembly, no
congestion control, no Nagle. Enough to echo-test against a
host echo server via `hostfwd=tcp`.

Tick budget assumes a ~100 Hz scheduler timer (10 ms per tick).

    val TCP_MAX_SOCKETS = 16
    val TCP_SEND_BUF    = 1024
    val TCP_RECV_BUF    = 1024
    val TCP_MSS_ADV     = 1460
    val TCP_MAX_SEG     = 480
    val TCP_RTO_TICKS   = 50
    val TCP_TW_TICKS    = 200
    val TCP_MAX_RETRIES = 5

    val TCP_STATE_CLOSED      = 0
    val TCP_STATE_SYN_SENT    = 1
    val TCP_STATE_ESTABLISHED = 2
    val TCP_STATE_FIN_WAIT_1  = 3
    val TCP_STATE_FIN_WAIT_2  = 4
    val TCP_STATE_CLOSE_WAIT  = 5
    val TCP_STATE_LAST_ACK    = 6
    val TCP_STATE_TIME_WAIT   = 7
    val TCP_STATE_LISTEN      = 8
    val TCP_STATE_SYN_RCVD    = 9

    val TCP_LISTEN_BACKLOG = 16

    val TCP_F_FIN = 0x01
    val TCP_F_SYN = 0x02
    val TCP_F_RST = 0x04
    val TCP_F_PSH = 0x08
    val TCP_F_ACK = 0x10

    struct TcpSocket
        in_use: int
        state: int
        owner_tid: int
        local_port: int
        remote_ip: u32
        remote_port: int
        iss: u32
        irs: u32
        snd_una: u32
        snd_nxt: u32
        snd_wnd: int
        rcv_nxt: u32
        mss: int
        send_buf: [1024]byte
        send_len: int
        recv_buf: [1024]byte
        recv_len: int
        rtx_deadline: int
        retries: int
        tw_deadline: int
        peer_fin: int
        our_fin_sent: int
        connect_waiter: int
        send_waiter: int
        send_waiter_len: int
        recv_waiter: int
        recv_maxlen: int
        close_waiter: int
        is_listen: int
        accept_queue: [16]int
        accept_head: int
        accept_tail: int
        accept_count: int
        accept_waiter: int
        parent_listen: int

    var tcp_sockets: [16]TcpSocket
    var tcp_iss_counter: u32 = u32(1000)

    tcp_next_iss() -> u32
        val v = tcp_iss_counter
        tcp_iss_counter = v + u32(65536)
        v

    inet_tcp_init()
        var i = 0
        while i < TCP_MAX_SOCKETS
            tcp_sockets[i].in_use = 0
            tcp_sockets[i].state = TCP_STATE_CLOSED
            tcp_sockets[i].connect_waiter = -1
            tcp_sockets[i].send_waiter = -1
            tcp_sockets[i].recv_waiter = -1
            tcp_sockets[i].close_waiter = -1
            tcp_sockets[i].is_listen = 0
            tcp_sockets[i].accept_head = 0
            tcp_sockets[i].accept_tail = 0
            tcp_sockets[i].accept_count = 0
            tcp_sockets[i].accept_waiter = -1
            tcp_sockets[i].parent_listen = -1
            i += 1


32-bit sequence-number comparisons, wrapping modulo 2^32.

    tcp_seq_lt(a: u32, b: u32) -> int
        val d = i32(a - b)
        if d < 0
            return 1
        0

    tcp_seq_le(a: u32, b: u32) -> int
        val d = i32(a - b)
        if d <= 0
            return 1
        0


TCP seq/ack field helpers (big-endian u32).

    tcp_write_u32(frame: *byte, off: int, v: u32)
        frame[off]     = byte((v >> 24) & u32(0xff))
        frame[off + 1] = byte((v >> 16) & u32(0xff))
        frame[off + 2] = byte((v >>  8) & u32(0xff))
        frame[off + 3] = byte( v        & u32(0xff))

    tcp_read_u32(frame: *byte, off: int) -> u32
        val b0 = u32(frame[off]     & 0xff)
        val b1 = u32(frame[off + 1] & 0xff)
        val b2 = u32(frame[off + 2] & 0xff)
        val b3 = u32(frame[off + 3] & 0xff)
        (b0 << 24) | (b1 << 16) | (b2 << 8) | b3


Build a single Ethernet + IPv4 + TCP frame for socket `s`. Payload
is `payload_len` bytes of send_buf starting at `payload_seq`
(relative to snd_una). A 4-byte MSS option is attached on SYN.

    inet_tcp_emit(s: int, flags: int, seq: u32,
                  payload_seq: u32, payload_len: int) -> int
        if inet_our_mac_known == 0
            return -1
        var next_hop_mac: [6]byte
        if inet_resolve_mac(tcp_sockets[s].remote_ip, next_hop_mac) == 0
            return -1
        val mss_opt = (flags & TCP_F_SYN) != 0
        var hdr_bytes = 20
        if mss_opt
            hdr_bytes = 24
        var seg_len = hdr_bytes + payload_len
        if seg_len > 1460
            return -1
        var frame: [1514]byte
        val total_len = 14 + 20 + seg_len
        pkt_write_mac(frame, 0, next_hop_mac)
        pkt_write_mac(frame, 6, inet_our_mac)
        pkt_write_u16(frame, 12, ETHERTYPE_IPV4)
        frame[14] = 0x45
        frame[15] = 0
        pkt_write_u16(frame, 16, 20 + seg_len)
        pkt_write_u16(frame, 18, 0)
        pkt_write_u16(frame, 20, 0x4000)
        frame[22] = 64
        frame[23] = byte(IP_PROTO_TCP)
        pkt_write_u16(frame, 24, 0)
        val our_ip = ipv4(INET_OUR_IP_A, INET_OUR_IP_B,
            INET_OUR_IP_C, INET_OUR_IP_D)
        pkt_write_ipv4(frame, 26,
            INET_OUR_IP_A, INET_OUR_IP_B, INET_OUR_IP_C, INET_OUR_IP_D)
        pkt_write_ipv4(frame, 30,
            ipv4_octet(tcp_sockets[s].remote_ip, 0),
            ipv4_octet(tcp_sockets[s].remote_ip, 1),
            ipv4_octet(tcp_sockets[s].remote_ip, 2),
            ipv4_octet(tcp_sockets[s].remote_ip, 3))
        pkt_write_u16(frame, 24, net_checksum(frame + 14, 20))
        val tcp_off = 34
        pkt_write_u16(frame, tcp_off + 0, tcp_sockets[s].local_port)
        pkt_write_u16(frame, tcp_off + 2, tcp_sockets[s].remote_port)
        tcp_write_u32(frame, tcp_off + 4, seq)
        var ack_val: u32 = u32(0)
        if (flags & TCP_F_ACK) != 0
            ack_val = tcp_sockets[s].rcv_nxt
        tcp_write_u32(frame, tcp_off + 8, ack_val)
        val data_off_words = hdr_bytes / 4
        frame[tcp_off + 12] = byte((data_off_words << 4) & 0xf0)
        frame[tcp_off + 13] = byte(flags & 0xff)
        val rwnd = TCP_RECV_BUF - tcp_sockets[s].recv_len
        pkt_write_u16(frame, tcp_off + 14, rwnd)
        pkt_write_u16(frame, tcp_off + 16, 0)
        pkt_write_u16(frame, tcp_off + 18, 0)
        if mss_opt
            frame[tcp_off + 20] = 2
            frame[tcp_off + 21] = 4
            pkt_write_u16(frame, tcp_off + 22, TCP_MSS_ADV)
        if payload_len > 0
            val offset = int(i32(payload_seq - tcp_sockets[s].snd_una))
            var i = 0
            while i < payload_len
                frame[tcp_off + hdr_bytes + i] = tcp_sockets[s].send_buf[offset + i]
                i += 1
        pkt_write_u16(frame, tcp_off + 16,
            (~inet_l4_partial_sum(our_ip, tcp_sockets[s].remote_ip,
                IP_PROTO_TCP, frame, tcp_off, seg_len)) & 0xffff)
        inet_nic_send_packet(frame, total_len)
        0


    inet_tcp_arm_rtx(s: int)
        tcp_sockets[s].rtx_deadline = int(uptime()) + TCP_RTO_TICKS

    inet_tcp_disarm_rtx(s: int)
        tcp_sockets[s].rtx_deadline = 0
        tcp_sockets[s].retries = 0


One-byte status reply — close() completion.

    inet_tcp_reply_status(tid: int, status: int)
        var wr: [1]byte
        wr[0] = byte(status & 0xff)
        ipc_reply(tid, wr, 1)


Two-byte connect() reply: status + fd. fd is meaningless on
error but the client still reads it (stable wire shape).

    inet_tcp_reply_connect(tid: int, status: int, fd: int)
        var wr: [2]byte
        wr[0] = byte(status & 0xff)
        wr[1] = byte(fd & 0xff)
        ipc_reply(tid, wr, 2)

Parked SEND reply (MVP currently doesn't park, keep helper for
symmetry / phase 2).

    inet_tcp_reply_send(tid: int, status: int, written: int)
        var wr: [3]byte
        wr[0] = byte(status & 0xff)
        pkt_write_u16(wr, 1, written)
        ipc_reply(tid, wr, 3)

RECV drain + reply. `n == 0` signals peer-closed EOF.

    inet_tcp_reply_recv(s: int, n: int)
        val tid = tcp_sockets[s].recv_waiter
        tcp_sockets[s].recv_waiter = -1
        var wr: [540]byte
        wr[0] = 0
        pkt_write_u16(wr, 1, n)
        var i = 0
        while i < n
            wr[3 + i] = tcp_sockets[s].recv_buf[i]
            i += 1
        if n > 0
            var j = n
            while j < tcp_sockets[s].recv_len
                tcp_sockets[s].recv_buf[j - n] = tcp_sockets[s].recv_buf[j]
                j += 1
            tcp_sockets[s].recv_len -= n
        ipc_reply(tid, wr, 3 + n)


Free socket `s` and wake any parked waiter with `status`. Used on
terminal ACK and on retransmit exhaustion.

Enter TIME_WAIT for 2MSL. Unblocks any parked close() caller
immediately (the handshake is complete from the app's point of
view) but leaves the slot live until tw_deadline fires — so the
stack can absorb a retransmitted peer FIN and stale duplicates.

    inet_tcp_enter_time_wait(s: int)
        if tcp_sockets[s].close_waiter >= 0
            inet_tcp_reply_status(tcp_sockets[s].close_waiter, 0)
            tcp_sockets[s].close_waiter = -1
        tcp_sockets[s].state = TCP_STATE_TIME_WAIT
        tcp_sockets[s].rtx_deadline = 0
        tcp_sockets[s].tw_deadline = int(uptime()) + TCP_TW_TICKS


    inet_tcp_close_slot(s: int, status: int)
        if tcp_sockets[s].connect_waiter >= 0
            inet_tcp_reply_connect(tcp_sockets[s].connect_waiter, status, 0)
            tcp_sockets[s].connect_waiter = -1
        if tcp_sockets[s].recv_waiter >= 0
            inet_tcp_reply_recv(s, 0)
        if tcp_sockets[s].send_waiter >= 0
            inet_tcp_reply_send(tcp_sockets[s].send_waiter, status, 0)
            tcp_sockets[s].send_waiter = -1
        if tcp_sockets[s].close_waiter >= 0
            inet_tcp_reply_status(tcp_sockets[s].close_waiter, 0)
            tcp_sockets[s].close_waiter = -1
        if tcp_sockets[s].accept_waiter >= 0
            inet_tcp_reply_accept(tcp_sockets[s].accept_waiter, status, 0)
            tcp_sockets[s].accept_waiter = -1
        tcp_sockets[s].in_use = 0
        tcp_sockets[s].state = TCP_STATE_CLOSED
        tcp_sockets[s].is_listen = 0
        tcp_sockets[s].accept_count = 0
        tcp_sockets[s].accept_head = 0
        tcp_sockets[s].accept_tail = 0
        tcp_sockets[s].parent_listen = -1
        tcp_sockets[s].rtx_deadline = 0
        tcp_sockets[s].tw_deadline = 0


    inet_tcp_alloc() -> int
        var i = 0
        while i < TCP_MAX_SOCKETS
            if tcp_sockets[i].in_use == 0
                tcp_sockets[i].in_use = 1
                tcp_sockets[i].state = TCP_STATE_CLOSED
                tcp_sockets[i].send_len = 0
                tcp_sockets[i].recv_len = 0
                tcp_sockets[i].retries = 0
                tcp_sockets[i].rtx_deadline = 0
                tcp_sockets[i].tw_deadline = 0
                tcp_sockets[i].peer_fin = 0
                tcp_sockets[i].our_fin_sent = 0
                tcp_sockets[i].connect_waiter = -1
                tcp_sockets[i].send_waiter = -1
                tcp_sockets[i].recv_waiter = -1
                tcp_sockets[i].close_waiter = -1
                tcp_sockets[i].mss = TCP_MSS_ADV
                tcp_sockets[i].is_listen = 0
                tcp_sockets[i].accept_head = 0
                tcp_sockets[i].accept_tail = 0
                tcp_sockets[i].accept_count = 0
                tcp_sockets[i].accept_waiter = -1
                tcp_sockets[i].parent_listen = -1
                return i
            i += 1
        -1

    inet_tcp_find(local_port: int, remote_ip: u32, remote_port: int) -> int
        var i = 0
        while i < TCP_MAX_SOCKETS
            if (tcp_sockets[i].in_use != 0 && tcp_sockets[i].is_listen == 0 &&
                    tcp_sockets[i].local_port == local_port &&
                    tcp_sockets[i].remote_port == remote_port &&
                    tcp_sockets[i].remote_ip == remote_ip)
                return i
            i += 1
        -1


Find a listen socket bound to `local_port`. Returns slot index or -1.

    inet_tcp_find_listen(local_port: int) -> int
        var i = 0
        while i < TCP_MAX_SOCKETS
            if (tcp_sockets[i].in_use != 0 && tcp_sockets[i].is_listen != 0 &&
                    tcp_sockets[i].local_port == local_port)
                return i
            i += 1
        -1


TCP-private ephemeral port allocator (49152+). Distinct from UDP's
so a TCP connect and a UDP socket can both hold 49152.

    tcp_alloc_port() -> int
        var port = 49152
        while port < 65536
            var taken = 0
            var i = 0
            while i < TCP_MAX_SOCKETS
                if tcp_sockets[i].in_use != 0
                    if tcp_sockets[i].local_port == port
                        taken = 1
                        i = TCP_MAX_SOCKETS
                    else
                        i += 1
                else
                    i += 1
            if taken == 0
                return port
            port += 1
        -1


connect() entry — allocate slot, emit SYN, park caller. Returns
the socket index on success (caller blocks until ESTABLISHED),
-1 on immediate failure.

    inet_tcp_begin_connect(owner_tid: int, caller_tid: int,
                           remote_ip: u32, remote_port: int) -> int
        if inet_our_mac_known == 0
            return -1
        val s = inet_tcp_alloc()
        if s < 0
            return -1
        val lp = tcp_alloc_port()
        if lp < 0
            tcp_sockets[s].in_use = 0
            return -1
        val iss = tcp_next_iss()
        tcp_sockets[s].owner_tid = owner_tid
        tcp_sockets[s].local_port = lp
        tcp_sockets[s].remote_ip = remote_ip
        tcp_sockets[s].remote_port = remote_port
        tcp_sockets[s].iss = iss
        tcp_sockets[s].snd_una = iss
        tcp_sockets[s].snd_nxt = iss + u32(1)
        tcp_sockets[s].rcv_nxt = u32(0)
        tcp_sockets[s].snd_wnd = 0
        tcp_sockets[s].state = TCP_STATE_SYN_SENT
        tcp_sockets[s].connect_waiter = caller_tid
        inet_tcp_emit(s, TCP_F_SYN, iss, u32(0), 0)
        inet_tcp_arm_rtx(s)
        s


listen() entry — allocate a slot bound to `local_port` in LISTEN
state. Unlike connect(), listen() returns immediately; the caller
reuses the returned fd for accept(). Fails with -1 if the slot
pool is exhausted or a listen is already bound to that port.

    inet_tcp_begin_listen(owner_tid: int, local_port: int) -> int
        if inet_tcp_find_listen(local_port) >= 0
            return -1
        val s = inet_tcp_alloc()
        if s < 0
            return -1
        tcp_sockets[s].owner_tid = owner_tid
        tcp_sockets[s].local_port = local_port
        tcp_sockets[s].remote_ip = u32(0)
        tcp_sockets[s].remote_port = 0
        tcp_sockets[s].state = TCP_STATE_LISTEN
        tcp_sockets[s].is_listen = 1
        s


Handle an incoming SYN that matches no existing 4-tuple but does
match a LISTEN socket. Allocates a child socket in SYN_RCVD,
emits SYN-ACK, arms retransmit. The child is NOT queued for
accept() until its SYN_RCVD → ESTABLISHED transition.

    inet_tcp_handle_passive_syn(ls: int, remote_ip: u32,
                                remote_port: int, seg_seq: u32)
        // If accept queue is already at capacity, silently drop.
        // SYN cookies / overflow handling is phase-3.
        if tcp_sockets[ls].accept_count >= TCP_LISTEN_BACKLOG
            return
        val s = inet_tcp_alloc()
        if s < 0
            return
        val iss = tcp_next_iss()
        tcp_sockets[s].owner_tid = tcp_sockets[ls].owner_tid
        tcp_sockets[s].local_port = tcp_sockets[ls].local_port
        tcp_sockets[s].remote_ip = remote_ip
        tcp_sockets[s].remote_port = remote_port
        tcp_sockets[s].iss = iss
        tcp_sockets[s].snd_una = iss
        tcp_sockets[s].snd_nxt = iss + u32(1)
        tcp_sockets[s].irs = seg_seq
        tcp_sockets[s].rcv_nxt = seg_seq + u32(1)
        tcp_sockets[s].snd_wnd = 0
        tcp_sockets[s].state = TCP_STATE_SYN_RCVD
        tcp_sockets[s].parent_listen = ls
        inet_tcp_emit(s, TCP_F_SYN | TCP_F_ACK, iss, u32(0), 0)
        inet_tcp_arm_rtx(s)


8-byte reply to a parked accept() caller:
status(1) + child_fd(1) + peer_ip(4) + peer_port(2).

    inet_tcp_reply_accept(tid: int, status: int, child_s: int)
        var wr: [8]byte
        wr[0] = byte(status & 0xff)
        wr[1] = byte(child_s & 0xff)
        if status == 0
            val rip = tcp_sockets[child_s].remote_ip
            wr[2] = byte(ipv4_octet(rip, 0) & 0xff)
            wr[3] = byte(ipv4_octet(rip, 1) & 0xff)
            wr[4] = byte(ipv4_octet(rip, 2) & 0xff)
            wr[5] = byte(ipv4_octet(rip, 3) & 0xff)
            pkt_write_u16(wr, 6, tcp_sockets[child_s].remote_port)
        ipc_reply(tid, wr, 8)


accept() entry — dequeue one established child (skipping dead
entries left behind by retransmit-giveup on a half-open child).
Returns the child socket index (caller replies immediately) or
-1 if the caller was parked as accept_waiter. Returns -2 if
`ls` is not a valid listen socket.

A child is also acceptable in CLOSE_WAIT: the peer can send data
and FIN while our accept() hasn't been called yet, so the child
transitions ESTABLISHED → CLOSE_WAIT before dequeue. Returning
it lets the caller drain buffered data and close cleanly instead
of silently dropping the connection. Other teardown states
(FIN_WAIT_*, LAST_ACK, TIME_WAIT) can't appear here — they only
enter after *we* close(), which the caller hasn't done yet.

    inet_tcp_do_accept(caller_tid: int, ls: int) -> int
        if tcp_sockets[ls].in_use == 0 || tcp_sockets[ls].is_listen == 0
            return -2
        while tcp_sockets[ls].accept_count > 0
            val head = tcp_sockets[ls].accept_head
            val c = tcp_sockets[ls].accept_queue[head]
            tcp_sockets[ls].accept_head = (head + 1) % TCP_LISTEN_BACKLOG
            tcp_sockets[ls].accept_count -= 1
            if tcp_sockets[c].in_use != 0
                val cst = tcp_sockets[c].state
                if cst == TCP_STATE_ESTABLISHED || cst == TCP_STATE_CLOSE_WAIT
                    return c
        // Queue empty — park caller.
        tcp_sockets[ls].accept_waiter = caller_tid
        -1


Enqueue a newly-established child onto its parent listen's accept
queue. If a caller is already parked in accept(), wake it with the
child directly (the entry is dequeued before reply, not after).

    inet_tcp_accept_enqueue(child_s: int)
        val ls = tcp_sockets[child_s].parent_listen
        if ls < 0 || tcp_sockets[ls].in_use == 0 || tcp_sockets[ls].is_listen == 0
            return
        if tcp_sockets[ls].accept_waiter >= 0
            val tid = tcp_sockets[ls].accept_waiter
            tcp_sockets[ls].accept_waiter = -1
            inet_tcp_reply_accept(tid, 0, child_s)
            return
        if tcp_sockets[ls].accept_count >= TCP_LISTEN_BACKLOG
            // Backlog full — the child becomes an orphan;
            // nobody will accept() it. Close it.
            inet_tcp_close_slot(child_s, -1)
            return
        val tail = tcp_sockets[ls].accept_tail
        tcp_sockets[ls].accept_queue[tail] = child_s
        tcp_sockets[ls].accept_tail = (tail + 1) % TCP_LISTEN_BACKLOG
        tcp_sockets[ls].accept_count += 1


Stateless RST emit for a segment arriving to a port with no
matching connection or listen socket. Per RFC 793 §3.4: if the
incoming segment has an ACK, the RST takes its seq from seg.ack
and no ACK flag; otherwise the RST has seq=0, ACK=seg.seq+seg_len,
and the ACK flag is set. seg_len counts SYN and FIN as one octet.

    inet_tcp_emit_rst(remote_ip: u32, remote_port: int,
                      local_port: int, seg_flags: int,
                      seg_seq: u32, seg_ack: u32, seg_payload_len: int)
        if inet_our_mac_known == 0
            return
        var next_hop_mac: [6]byte
        if inet_resolve_mac(remote_ip, next_hop_mac) == 0
            return
        var rst_seq: u32 = u32(0)
        var rst_ack: u32 = u32(0)
        var rst_flags = TCP_F_RST
        if (seg_flags & TCP_F_ACK) != 0
            rst_seq = seg_ack
        else
            var ack_bump = seg_payload_len
            if (seg_flags & TCP_F_SYN) != 0
                ack_bump += 1
            if (seg_flags & TCP_F_FIN) != 0
                ack_bump += 1
            rst_ack = seg_seq + u32(ack_bump)
            rst_flags = TCP_F_RST | TCP_F_ACK
        val hdr_bytes = 20
        val seg_total = hdr_bytes
        var frame: [1514]byte
        val total_len = 14 + 20 + seg_total
        pkt_write_mac(frame, 0, next_hop_mac)
        pkt_write_mac(frame, 6, inet_our_mac)
        pkt_write_u16(frame, 12, ETHERTYPE_IPV4)
        frame[14] = 0x45
        frame[15] = 0
        pkt_write_u16(frame, 16, 20 + seg_total)
        pkt_write_u16(frame, 18, 0)
        pkt_write_u16(frame, 20, 0x4000)
        frame[22] = 64
        frame[23] = byte(IP_PROTO_TCP)
        pkt_write_u16(frame, 24, 0)
        val our_ip = ipv4(INET_OUR_IP_A, INET_OUR_IP_B,
            INET_OUR_IP_C, INET_OUR_IP_D)
        pkt_write_ipv4(frame, 26,
            INET_OUR_IP_A, INET_OUR_IP_B, INET_OUR_IP_C, INET_OUR_IP_D)
        pkt_write_ipv4(frame, 30,
            ipv4_octet(remote_ip, 0), ipv4_octet(remote_ip, 1),
            ipv4_octet(remote_ip, 2), ipv4_octet(remote_ip, 3))
        pkt_write_u16(frame, 24, net_checksum(frame + 14, 20))
        val tcp_off = 34
        pkt_write_u16(frame, tcp_off + 0, local_port)
        pkt_write_u16(frame, tcp_off + 2, remote_port)
        tcp_write_u32(frame, tcp_off + 4, rst_seq)
        tcp_write_u32(frame, tcp_off + 8, rst_ack)
        frame[tcp_off + 12] = byte((5 << 4) & 0xf0)
        frame[tcp_off + 13] = byte(rst_flags & 0xff)
        pkt_write_u16(frame, tcp_off + 14, 0)
        pkt_write_u16(frame, tcp_off + 16, 0)
        pkt_write_u16(frame, tcp_off + 18, 0)
        pkt_write_u16(frame, tcp_off + 16,
            (~inet_l4_partial_sum(our_ip, remote_ip,
                IP_PROTO_TCP, frame, tcp_off, seg_total)) & 0xffff)
        inet_nic_send_packet(frame, total_len)


send() entry — buffer, emit one segment, reply bytes written.
Returns `n` on success (>= 0), -1 if connection is not
established. MVP rejects overlapping sends with written = 0.

    inet_tcp_do_send(s: int, data: *byte, len: int) -> int
        if tcp_sockets[s].state != TCP_STATE_ESTABLISHED
            return -1
        if tcp_sockets[s].send_len > 0
            return 0
        var n = len
        if n > TCP_SEND_BUF
            n = TCP_SEND_BUF
        if n > TCP_MAX_SEG
            n = TCP_MAX_SEG
        var i = 0
        while i < n
            tcp_sockets[s].send_buf[i] = data[i]
            i += 1
        tcp_sockets[s].send_len = n
        val seq = tcp_sockets[s].snd_nxt
        tcp_sockets[s].snd_nxt = seq + u32(n)
        inet_tcp_emit(s, TCP_F_ACK | TCP_F_PSH, seq, seq, n)
        inet_tcp_arm_rtx(s)
        n


close() entry — emit FIN (or immediately free if never opened).
Returns 0 if FIN is in-flight (caller blocks), 1 if already done,
-1 on invalid state.

    inet_tcp_do_close(s: int, caller_tid: int) -> int
        val st = tcp_sockets[s].state
        if st == TCP_STATE_CLOSED
            tcp_sockets[s].in_use = 0
            return 1
        if st == TCP_STATE_LISTEN
            // No peer to FIN; any parked accept_waiter gets woken
            // with status=1 (error) by close_slot.
            inet_tcp_close_slot(s, 1)
            return 1
        if st == TCP_STATE_ESTABLISHED
            val seq = tcp_sockets[s].snd_nxt
            tcp_sockets[s].snd_nxt = seq + u32(1)
            tcp_sockets[s].our_fin_sent = 1
            tcp_sockets[s].state = TCP_STATE_FIN_WAIT_1
            tcp_sockets[s].close_waiter = caller_tid
            inet_tcp_emit(s, TCP_F_ACK | TCP_F_FIN, seq, seq, 0)
            inet_tcp_arm_rtx(s)
            return 0
        if st == TCP_STATE_CLOSE_WAIT
            val seq = tcp_sockets[s].snd_nxt
            tcp_sockets[s].snd_nxt = seq + u32(1)
            tcp_sockets[s].our_fin_sent = 1
            tcp_sockets[s].state = TCP_STATE_LAST_ACK
            tcp_sockets[s].close_waiter = caller_tid
            inet_tcp_emit(s, TCP_F_ACK | TCP_F_FIN, seq, seq, 0)
            inet_tcp_arm_rtx(s)
            return 0
        if st == TCP_STATE_SYN_SENT
            inet_tcp_close_slot(s, -1)
            return 1
        -1


Inbound IPv4 protocol=6 dispatch. Parses header, verifies
checksum, locates the matching socket, and delegates.

    inet_tcp_handle_segment(frame: *byte, total_len: int, ihl_bytes: int)
        val tcp_off = 14 + ihl_bytes
        if total_len < tcp_off + 20
            return
        val src_port = pkt_read_u16(frame, tcp_off + 0)
        val dst_port = pkt_read_u16(frame, tcp_off + 2)
        val seq = tcp_read_u32(frame, tcp_off + 4)
        val ack = tcp_read_u32(frame, tcp_off + 8)
        val data_off_words = (int(frame[tcp_off + 12]) >> 4) & 0x0f
        val tcp_hdr_len = data_off_words * 4
        val flags = int(frame[tcp_off + 13]) & 0xff
        val wnd = pkt_read_u16(frame, tcp_off + 14)
        if tcp_hdr_len < 20
            return
        if total_len < tcp_off + tcp_hdr_len
            return
        val ip_total = pkt_read_u16(frame, 16)
        val tcp_len = ip_total - ihl_bytes
        val payload_len = tcp_len - tcp_hdr_len
        val payload: *byte = frame + tcp_off + tcp_hdr_len
        val src_ip = ipv4(
            int(frame[14 + 12]) & 0xff, int(frame[14 + 13]) & 0xff,
            int(frame[14 + 14]) & 0xff, int(frame[14 + 15]) & 0xff)
        val our_ip = ipv4(INET_OUR_IP_A, INET_OUR_IP_B,
            INET_OUR_IP_C, INET_OUR_IP_D)
        if inet_l4_partial_sum(src_ip, our_ip, IP_PROTO_TCP,
                frame, tcp_off, tcp_len) != 0xffff
            return
        val s = inet_tcp_find(dst_port, src_ip, src_port)
        if s < 0
            // No connection match. SYN-to-a-listen gets the passive
            // open path. Anything else that isn't already a RST gets
            // a stateless RST per RFC 793 §3.4.
            if (flags & TCP_F_RST) != 0
                return
            if (flags & TCP_F_SYN) != 0
                val ls = inet_tcp_find_listen(dst_port)
                if ls >= 0
                    inet_tcp_handle_passive_syn(ls, src_ip, src_port, seq)
                    return
            inet_tcp_emit_rst(src_ip, src_port, dst_port,
                              flags, seq, ack, payload_len)
            return
        inet_tcp_state_step(s, flags, seq, ack, wnd, payload, payload_len)


Per-socket state transition for one validated segment.

    inet_tcp_state_step(s: int, flags: int, seq: u32, ack: u32,
                        wnd: int, payload: *byte, payload_len: int)
        val st = tcp_sockets[s].state
        if st == TCP_STATE_SYN_SENT
            if (flags & TCP_F_RST) != 0
                inet_tcp_close_slot(s, -1)
                return
            if (flags & TCP_F_SYN) == 0
                return
            if (flags & TCP_F_ACK) == 0
                return
            if ack != tcp_sockets[s].snd_nxt
                return
            tcp_sockets[s].irs = seq
            tcp_sockets[s].rcv_nxt = seq + u32(1)
            tcp_sockets[s].snd_una = ack
            tcp_sockets[s].snd_wnd = wnd
            tcp_sockets[s].state = TCP_STATE_ESTABLISHED
            inet_tcp_disarm_rtx(s)
            inet_tcp_emit(s, TCP_F_ACK, tcp_sockets[s].snd_nxt, u32(0), 0)
            if tcp_sockets[s].connect_waiter >= 0
                inet_tcp_reply_connect(tcp_sockets[s].connect_waiter, 0, s)
                tcp_sockets[s].connect_waiter = -1
            return
        if st == TCP_STATE_SYN_RCVD
            if (flags & TCP_F_RST) != 0
                inet_tcp_close_slot(s, -1)
                return
            if (flags & TCP_F_ACK) == 0
                return
            if ack != tcp_sockets[s].snd_nxt
                return
            tcp_sockets[s].snd_una = ack
            tcp_sockets[s].snd_wnd = wnd
            tcp_sockets[s].state = TCP_STATE_ESTABLISHED
            inet_tcp_disarm_rtx(s)
            // Hand child to parent listen (or directly to the parked
            // accept caller). Data in this segment is ignored — rely on
            // the peer retransmitting once we ACK the next segment.
            inet_tcp_accept_enqueue(s)
            return

Past handshake: process ACK, data, FIN in that order.

        if (flags & TCP_F_RST) != 0
            inet_tcp_close_slot(s, -1)
            return
        if (flags & TCP_F_ACK) != 0
            if tcp_seq_lt(tcp_sockets[s].snd_una, ack) != 0
                if tcp_seq_le(ack, tcp_sockets[s].snd_nxt) != 0
                    val acked = int(i32(ack - tcp_sockets[s].snd_una))
                    var eff = acked
                    if tcp_sockets[s].our_fin_sent != 0
                        if ack == tcp_sockets[s].snd_nxt
                            eff -= 1
                    if eff > tcp_sockets[s].send_len
                        eff = tcp_sockets[s].send_len
                    var k = eff
                    while k < tcp_sockets[s].send_len
                        tcp_sockets[s].send_buf[k - eff] = tcp_sockets[s].send_buf[k]
                        k += 1
                    tcp_sockets[s].send_len -= eff
                    tcp_sockets[s].snd_una = ack
                    tcp_sockets[s].snd_wnd = wnd
                    if tcp_sockets[s].snd_una == tcp_sockets[s].snd_nxt
                        inet_tcp_disarm_rtx(s)

        var did_data = 0
        if payload_len > 0
            if seq == tcp_sockets[s].rcv_nxt
                val room = TCP_RECV_BUF - tcp_sockets[s].recv_len
                var take = payload_len
                if take > room
                    take = room
                var i = 0
                while i < take
                    tcp_sockets[s].recv_buf[tcp_sockets[s].recv_len + i] = payload[i]
                    i += 1
                tcp_sockets[s].recv_len += take
                tcp_sockets[s].rcv_nxt = tcp_sockets[s].rcv_nxt + u32(take)
                did_data = 1

        var did_fin = 0
        if (flags & TCP_F_FIN) != 0
            if seq + u32(payload_len) == tcp_sockets[s].rcv_nxt
                tcp_sockets[s].rcv_nxt = tcp_sockets[s].rcv_nxt + u32(1)
                tcp_sockets[s].peer_fin = 1
                did_fin = 1

        if did_data != 0
            inet_tcp_emit(s, TCP_F_ACK, tcp_sockets[s].snd_nxt, u32(0), 0)
            if tcp_sockets[s].recv_waiter >= 0
                val mx = tcp_sockets[s].recv_maxlen
                var give = tcp_sockets[s].recv_len
                if give > mx
                    give = mx
                inet_tcp_reply_recv(s, give)
        if did_fin != 0
            inet_tcp_emit(s, TCP_F_ACK, tcp_sockets[s].snd_nxt, u32(0), 0)

        val st2 = tcp_sockets[s].state
        if st2 == TCP_STATE_ESTABLISHED
            if did_fin != 0
                tcp_sockets[s].state = TCP_STATE_CLOSE_WAIT
                if tcp_sockets[s].recv_waiter >= 0
                    if tcp_sockets[s].recv_len == 0
                        inet_tcp_reply_recv(s, 0)
        else if st2 == TCP_STATE_FIN_WAIT_1
            if tcp_sockets[s].snd_una == tcp_sockets[s].snd_nxt
                if did_fin != 0
                    // Simultaneous close: peer FIN arrived with the ACK
                    // of our FIN. Enter TIME_WAIT for 2MSL.
                    inet_tcp_enter_time_wait(s)
                else
                    tcp_sockets[s].state = TCP_STATE_FIN_WAIT_2
        else if st2 == TCP_STATE_FIN_WAIT_2
            if did_fin != 0
                // Peer FIN after our FIN-ACK — enter TIME_WAIT.
                inet_tcp_enter_time_wait(s)
        else if st2 == TCP_STATE_LAST_ACK
            if tcp_sockets[s].snd_una == tcp_sockets[s].snd_nxt
                inet_tcp_close_slot(s, 0)


Called from inet main loop on every wake. Scans every active
socket for retransmit and TIME_WAIT deadlines.

    inet_tcp_scan_timers()
        val now = int(uptime())
        var i = 0
        while i < TCP_MAX_SOCKETS
            if tcp_sockets[i].in_use != 0
                val rtx = tcp_sockets[i].rtx_deadline
                if rtx != 0
                    if now >= rtx
                        if tcp_sockets[i].retries >= TCP_MAX_RETRIES
                            inet_tcp_close_slot(i, -1)
                        else
                            tcp_sockets[i].retries += 1
                            inet_tcp_retransmit(i)
                            inet_tcp_arm_rtx(i)
                val tw = tcp_sockets[i].tw_deadline
                if tw != 0
                    if now >= tw
                        inet_tcp_close_slot(i, 0)
            i += 1

    inet_tcp_retransmit(s: int)
        val st = tcp_sockets[s].state
        if st == TCP_STATE_SYN_SENT
            inet_tcp_emit(s, TCP_F_SYN, tcp_sockets[s].iss, u32(0), 0)
            return
        if st == TCP_STATE_SYN_RCVD
            inet_tcp_emit(s, TCP_F_SYN | TCP_F_ACK, tcp_sockets[s].iss, u32(0), 0)
            return
        if st == TCP_STATE_ESTABLISHED
            if tcp_sockets[s].send_len > 0
                inet_tcp_emit(s, TCP_F_ACK | TCP_F_PSH,
                    tcp_sockets[s].snd_una, tcp_sockets[s].snd_una,
                    tcp_sockets[s].send_len)
            return
        if st == TCP_STATE_FIN_WAIT_1
            inet_tcp_emit(s, TCP_F_ACK | TCP_F_FIN,
                tcp_sockets[s].snd_nxt - u32(1), u32(0), 0)
            return
        if st == TCP_STATE_LAST_ACK
            inet_tcp_emit(s, TCP_F_ACK | TCP_F_FIN,
                tcp_sockets[s].snd_nxt - u32(1), u32(0), 0)
            return
